IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wpa-types`

-- Wages Protection Act 1983 — GOAL 1: WAS THIS DEDUCTION LAWFUL?
--
--   "May the employer make this deduction from the worker's wages — under
--    the worker's written consent or request (ss 5, 5A), as recovery of an
--    overpayment (s 6), or under another Act, a collective agreement or an
--    order (ss 15, 16)?"
--
-- Source: ../source/WPA1983.txt — ss 4, 5, 5A, 6, 15, 16; Schedule cl 2.

§ `Goal 1 — deductions and overpayments`

§§ `Dates`

-- Schedule cl 2(2) "The amendments made by the 2016 Act do not apply to
-- conduct that occurred before the commencement of that Act" (1 April 2016:
-- ss 5(1), 5(1A), 5A, 11, 11A, 12A(1), 13 were replaced, inserted or
-- amended). The sections as they stood before are not carried.
@ref Schedule cls 1-2
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` d IF
    d AT LEAST Date 1 4 2016

@ref Schedule cl 2
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry` MEANS
    REFUSE "conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry"

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- ss 5(2), 9(2): the employer must act on a notice of withdrawal "(a) within
-- 2 weeks of receiving that notice, if practicable; and (b) as soon as is
-- practicable, in every other case". FORK F1: the consent or request still
-- covers what the employer does up to and including that last day.
@ref ss 5(2), 9(2)
GIVEN n IS A `Notice of withdrawal`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the employer may act on the old consent, after` n MEANS
    IF n's `practicable to act on within 2 weeks`
    THEN `the day` 14 `days after` (n's `received by the employer on`)
    ELSE n's `earliest practicable day to act on it`

@ref ss 5(2), 9(2)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, w IS A MAYBE `Notice of withdrawal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent or request still covers what is done on` d `, notice` w IF
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN JUST n THEN d AT MOST `the last day the employer may act on the old consent, after` n
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

§§ `Overpayments (s 6)`

-- s 6(1) "overpayment means any wages paid to a worker in respect of a
-- recoverable period", a period for which no wages are payable because the
-- worker was absent without authority, on strike, locked out or suspended.
@ref s 6(1)
GIVEN o IS AN Overpayment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an overpayment within s 6(1)` o IF
    NOT o's `reason no wages were payable for the period` EQUALS `none of these`

-- s 6(4)(a): a notice is not invalid because "it does not specify the amount
-- of the overpayment concerned but specifies only the day on which that
-- overpayment was made and the actions that led to its being an
-- overpayment". (4)(b), the group notice, needs no rule: such a notice is
-- valid for the worker it was given to.
@ref s 6(3)(b), (4)
GIVEN n IS AN `Overpayment notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice identifies the overpayment` n IF
        n's `specifies the amount`
    OR  n's `specifies the day of the overpayment and the actions that made it one`

-- s 6(3)(c): the last day for the notice of "any other overpayment".
@ref s 6(3)(c)
GIVEN o IS AN Overpayment
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for notice of the overpayment` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o's `workplace`
    WHEN `(i) no fixed workplace` THEN `the day` 10 `days after` (o's `next pay day`)
    WHEN `(ii) one fixed workplace, not attended during normal hours on the next pay day` first THEN first
    WHEN `(iii) 2 or more fixed workplaces, none attended during normal hours on the next pay day` first THEN first
    WHEN `(iv) any other case` THEN o's `next pay day`

-- s 6(3) "No employer shall recover an overpayment under subsection (2)
-- unless— (a) ... it was not reasonably practicable for that employer to
-- avoid making that overpayment; and (b) before recovering that overpayment,
-- that employer gives that worker notice ...; and (ba) in the case of an
-- overpayment that relates to a specified pay deduction, that notice— (i) is
-- given no later than 10 working days after the pay day on which the
-- overpayment was made; and (ii) specifies the method ...; and (c) in the
-- case of any other overpayment, that notice is given— [the s 6(3)(c) day];
-- and (d) that overpayment is recovered not later than 2 months after that
-- notice is given." FORK F2: notice given on the day of recovery is given
-- "before recovering". The working-day count in (ba)(i) is an input.
@ref s 6(1)-(4)
@export Whether an employer may recover an overpayment of wages from later wages under s 6 of the Wages Protection Act 1983 (NZ): the wages must have been paid for a period when none were payable (absence without authority, strike, lockout, suspension); the overpayment must not have been reasonably avoidable; notice must be given before recovery and in time (10 working days for a specified pay deduction, with the s 95C method; otherwise by the s 6(3)(c) day); and recovery must be within 2 months of the notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN Overpayment  @desc The overpayment: amount, why no wages were payable, whether it relates to a specified pay deduction, whether it was avoidable, pay days, the worker's workplace, the notice and the recovery date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` o IF
        `an overpayment within s 6(1)` o
    AND o's `not reasonably practicable to avoid, given the employer's usual payroll methods`
    AND CONSIDER o's `notice`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST n THEN
                `the notice identifies the overpayment` n
            AND n's `given on` AT MOST o's `recovered on`
            AND (IF o's `relates to a specified pay deduction (ERA s 82AA)`
                 THEN     n's `working days from the overpayment pay day to the notice` AT MOST 10
                      AND n's `specifies the s 95C method used to calculate the deduction`
                 ELSE n's `given on` AT MOST `the last day for notice of the overpayment` o)
            AND o's `recovered on` AT MOST `add months` (n's `given on`) 2

§§ `Deductions (ss 4, 5, 5A, 15, 16)`

-- s 5(1) "An employer may, for a lawful purpose, make deductions from wages
-- payable to a worker— (a) with the written consent of the worker (including
-- consent in a general deductions clause in the worker's employment
-- agreement); or (b) on the written request of the worker." (1A) no specific
-- deduction under a general deductions clause "without first consulting the
-- worker". s 5A "must not make a deduction under section 5 ... if the
-- deduction is unreasonable". s 5(2): a withdrawn consent stops covering
-- deductions after the s 5(2) day. A consent or request "obtained by threat
-- of dismissal, or otherwise by duress" (s 11(1)(a)(ii)) is not a consent.
@ref ss 5(1), (1A), (2), 5A
GIVEN `general clause` IS A BOOLEAN, duress IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A Deduction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction is within ss 5 and 5A, general clause:` `general clause` `, duress:` duress `, deduction` d IF
        NOT duress
    AND d's `for a lawful purpose`
    AND ((NOT `general clause`) OR d's `the worker was consulted before the deduction`)
    AND NOT d's `unreasonable`
    AND `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (d's `made on`) `, notice` (d's `notice of withdrawal`)

-- s 4 "Subject to sections 5(1) and 6(2), an employer shall, when any wages
-- become payable to a worker, pay the entire amount of those wages to that
-- worker without deduction." s 15: the Act is "read subject to the
-- provisions of any other Act"; s 16: nothing in it derogates from a
-- collective agreement or an order of the Court or Authority.
@ref ss 4, 5, 5A, 6(2), 15, 16
GIVEN d IS A Deduction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basis relied on allows the deduction` d IF
    CONSIDER d's `basis`
    WHEN `the worker's written consent` general duress THEN
        `the deduction is within ss 5 and 5A, general clause:` general `, duress:` duress `, deduction` d
    WHEN `the worker's written request` duress THEN
        `the deduction is within ss 5 and 5A, general clause:` FALSE `, duress:` duress `, deduction` d
    WHEN `recovery of an overpayment under s 6` o THEN `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` o
    WHEN `required or authorised by another Act (s 15)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a collective agreement or an order of the Court or Authority (s 16)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no written consent or request` THEN FALSE

-- How much of the deduction is lawful. s 6(2) lets the employer "recover the
-- amount of that overpayment", so a s 6 deduction is lawful only up to the
-- overpayment; anything above it is a deduction s 4 forbids. Raised by the
-- independent test author.
@ref ss 4, 5, 5A, 6(2), 15, 16; Schedule cl 2
GIVEN d IS A Deduction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lawful part of the deduction` d MEANS
    IF NOT `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` (d's `made on`)
    THEN `the lawful part of a deduction before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry`
    ELSE IF `the basis relied on allows the deduction` d
         THEN CONSIDER d's `basis`
              WHEN `recovery of an overpayment under s 6` o THEN min (d's `amount`) (o's `amount`)
              OTHERWISE d's `amount`
         ELSE 0

@ref Schedule cl 2
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lawful part of a deduction before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry` MEANS
    REFUSE "conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry"

@ref ss 4, 5, 5A, 6(2), 15, 16; Schedule cl 2
@export Whether a deduction from a worker's wages was lawful under the Wages Protection Act 1983 (NZ): s 4 forbids deductions except with the worker's written consent or request, for a lawful purpose, after consultation where made under a general deductions clause, and not unreasonable (ss 5, 5A); or as recovery of an overpayment under s 6, up to the amount overpaid; or under another Act, a collective agreement, or an order of the Court or Authority (ss 15, 16). Deductions before 1 April 2016 are outside the Act as it now stands. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A Deduction  @desc The deduction: amount, date, what the employer relied on (consent, request, s 6 overpayment, another Act, collective agreement), lawful purpose, consultation, whether unreasonable, and any notice withdrawing the consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the deduction was lawful` d MEANS
    `the lawful part of the deduction` d EQUALS d's `amount`
